calls</span><span class="stat-value">0 <span class="stat-sub">(0 err)</span></span></div><div class="stat"><span class="stat-label">Dispatches</span><span class="stat-value">0</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="stat-label">Active time <span class="stat-sub">(session grain — not split per case, stage or dispatch)</span></span><span class="stat-value">0.0h</span></div></div></div></section>
  
  
  
  
  <section class="panel"><h2>Per case — direct, measured (tokens: no per-dispatch dollars on this host)</h2>
  <p class="panel-sub">Batch overhead is NOT in these bars — it is the labelled figure above, shown once instead of smeared. Clustered cases are an even split of their shared dispatches. Loaded minutes are batch time ÷ cases (session grain), an allocation.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="panel"><h2>Spread</h2>
  <p>Tokens: n/a<br>Active time: session grain, none per case</p></section>
  
  
  
